- op: discuss  # 2082
  at: '2026-09-18T19:41:30Z'  # 2082
  by: agent  # 2082
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2082
  clock: 3  # 2082
  nonce: '2082'  # 2082
  message: "ADR-0057 (2026-09-18) relocates this row's cure: the merged record's span is the ITEM span (enclosing_range) and that fold happens INSIDE the merge pass, WI-kokiz-tilam-bohos-tivat-fogil-bijoj-munad-gazid — not as a standalone index.py edit. WI-kokiz-tilam-bohos-tivat-fogil-bijoj-munad-gazid now blocks this row.\n\nCORRECTION to my 2026-09-18 filing: the clause \"split_within_file_stable_id_collisions would re-mint the SCIP record as a second SITE\" holds only if the span fold lands WITHOUT a merge. Under ADR-0057 §8 the merge runs first, so no same-(path, stable_id) cross-backend group ever reaches the splitter; the splitter is untouched. The invariant (SCIP Symbol.span is the token) remains VIOLATED until the merge ships; do not close on this note."  # 2082
- op: discuss  # aeb1
  at: '2026-09-19T04:11:10Z'  # aeb1
  by: agent  # aeb1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # aeb1
  clock: 4  # aeb1
  nonce: aeb1  # aeb1
  message: "PARTIAL CURE LANDED (WI-kokiz, the merge pass): every SCIP record that pairs with a tree-sitter record is folded into a merged record whose span is the ITEM span (148 of 169 on the recorded aardvark-dns fixture; multi-line on every multi-line callable). The invariant remains VIOLATED for the 21 SCIP-only leftovers (18 namespaces, 2 type aliases, 1 static — see WI-bamar for why the incumbent has no record to fold them into): their Symbol.span is still the identifier token, because scip/index.py spans from the Definition `range` and the merge has no partner span to take. Closing this row means spanning SCIP-only records from enclosing_range in index.py — which is now safe under ADR-0057 §8 (the merge runs first, so no cross-backend (path, stable_id) group reaches the collision splitter). Not done here: it is a separate importer change with its own measurement (the 21 leftovers' spans before/after)."  # aeb1
