- op: discuss  # 12ac
  at: '2026-10-03T06:22:55Z'  # 12ac
  by: agent  # 12ac
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 12ac
  clock: 6  # 12ac
  nonce: 12ac  # 12ac
  message: "Owner-approved (2026-10-03): removed WI-gojum's isbefore link to this item, and dropped \"-- gated on WI-gojum\" from the title. The gate no longer applies:\n- ADR-0057 §8: split_within_file_stable_id_collisions runs AFTER the merge pass, so the clause \"the splitter would re-mint the SCIP record\" does not arise.\n- ADR-0057 §3 / §Tracker items: the merge pass (WI-kokiz, landed) already gives every MERGED record the item span (enclosing_range). On the recorded aardvark-dns index, all 148 merged records carry the item span after the merge.\n- What remains is independent of WI-gojum (still parked by the owner): the SCIP-only leftovers. On aardvark-dns, 21 records stay SCIP-only, and 5 of them have range != enclosing_range: ThreadHandleMap, DNSBACKEND, AardvarkResult and two inline `mod tests` namespaces. The other 16 are file-level namespaces whose range already equals enclosing_range. The 09-19 note's \"all 21 keep the token span\" overstates this.\n- Cure location (audit 2026-10-03): index.py runs BEFORE the merge, so re-spanning there cannot target only the leftovers. Both SCIP backends declare span_role=SPAN_ROLE_TOKEN (rust-analyzer analyzer.py:187, scip-python analyzer.py:137), and _spans_pair pairs token-inside-item, so re-spanning every SCIP record in index.py would break the declared anchor. The cure belongs AFTER the merge: re-span the unpaired records from enclosing_range carried in meta. Or it comes with an anchor change to ITEM plus a re-measure of the 148 pairs. scip-python fills enclosing_range on only 8 of 24 definitions in its recorded sample, so a re-span from enclosing_range cannot reach every leftover there."  # 12ac
